The two zigzag theorems (lines 25–90 and 186–241) have the same homotopical tail. It starts at `have := kq.twoOutOfThree` and ends at `MorphismProperty.of_retract hr hvW`. The tail contains:
- the instance setup for `ContainsIdentities` and `IsStableUnderRetracts`;
- the argument that `endpoint true ≫ U` is a weak equivalence, because `endpoint false ≫ U = 𝟙`;
- the transfer along `huv` to `V`, which shows `p ≫ j` is a weak equivalence;
- the retract square exhibiting `j` as a retract of `p ≫ j`.
The finite theorem repeats it verbatim with `.val`/`inclusion.map` decorations. A fix to this reasoning has to be made twice.
